pySMESH: OCCGeometry::Save refuses STL output instead of writing it through StlAPI_Writer
(netgen 6.2.2101; applies after 0005-occt-8.0-netgen-occ.patch).

Why: StlAPI_Writer lives in OCCT's TKDESTL. Save is virtual (basegeom.hpp:208, occgeom.hpp
:281), so the vtable of OCCGeometry references it, and every binary that builds an
OCCGeometry imports TKDESTL.dll: measured on v2_probe.exe, whose only TKDESTL imports are
the StlAPI_Writer constructor and StlAPI_Writer::Write. NETGENPlugin builds an OCCGeometry
for every compute, so _core.pyd would import TKDESTL.dll and the wheel would ship one more
DLL. pySMESH never saves a netgen geometry: netgen writes geometry files from its GUI and
its Python module only, and pySMESH builds neither.

Change, in libsrc/occ/occgeom.cpp only: the two STL branches of OCCGeometry::Save (".stl"
ASCII and ".stlb" binary) become one branch that throws NgException, naming the reason.
The IGES and STEP branches do not change: their writers live in TKDEIGES and TKDESTEP,
which _core.pyd imports already. Nothing that meshes calls Save, so no mesh changes.

diff --git a/libsrc/occ/occgeom.cpp b/libsrc/occ/occgeom.cpp
--- a/libsrc/occ/occgeom.cpp
+++ b/libsrc/occ/occgeom.cpp
@@ -1699,17 +1699,11 @@
 	writer.Transfer (shape, STEPControl_AsIs);
 	writer.Write (filename);
       }
-    else if (strcmp (&filename[strlen(filename)-3], "stl") == 0)
-      {
-	StlAPI_Writer writer;
-	writer.ASCIIMode() = Standard_True;
-	writer.Write (shape, filename);
-      }
-    else if (strcmp (&filename[strlen(filename)-4], "stlb") == 0)
-      {
-	StlAPI_Writer writer;
-	writer.ASCIIMode() = Standard_False;
-	writer.Write (shape, filename);
+    else if (strcmp (&filename[strlen(filename)-3], "stl") == 0 ||
+             strcmp (&filename[strlen(filename)-4], "stlb") == 0)
+      {
+	// pySMESH: STL output needs OCCT's TKDESTL, which the pySMESH wheel does not ship.
+	throw NgException ("OCCGeometry::Save: STL output is not built into pySMESH");
       }
   }
 
